  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be the values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>&nbsp;for which the points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;are at equal distance&nbsp; from the plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>then the distance of the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;from the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi></math></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "9",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be the values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>&nbsp;for which the points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;are at equal distance&nbsp; from the plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></math>,</p><p>So, by using distance formula of a point from a plane we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><msqrt><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><msqrt><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Now finding the distance of point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;from the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0107_ef1a75480e28.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 251px;\" /></p><p>Now form diagram we can see that,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;is perpendicular to given line,</p><p>So, by perpendicular condition we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>or</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Hence, the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp;will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So, the distance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}